              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Aerospace Material Specifications (AMS) are established by the Society of Automotive Engineers (SAE). Compiled in a comprehensive database of individual directives, AMS specifications cover materials, material tolerances, and quality control procedures and processes. AMS specifications are created or updated to align with the advances in material science and processes technologies within the Aerospace industry."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Global aerospace engineering standards are vital to the certification of an aircrafts airworthiness and interoperability. The AMS database consists of over 8,500 aerospace standards currently active and the documents create commonality between processes and procedures, practices, and the manufacturing of products throughout the aerospace industry."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "AMS specifications list chemical composition, detailed technical requirements, and cross reference similar specifications and materials, like corrosion and heat resistant steels, alloy steels, cast iron, aluminum, magnesium, copper, titanium, and other nonferrous alloys, special property and reactive materials, and non-metallic materials."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Below is a list of the products carried in our inventory that conform to AMS specifications ."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Disclaimer The use of this information should be considered strictly voluntary. Information contained in this page or across the domain, may contain typographical errors and are for reference only. Information presented are purely generalizations and are not a substitution for AMS specifications."
                },
